From dc2efa4cedf1f85391cc928c28123d9c2493440d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add The Hex item-upgrade system and redesign every menu

The Hex (/hex) is an item-upgrade hub modelled on Hypixel Skyblock's Hex.
Players bank essence, then spend essence and coins to raise an item's Hex
tier, add Master Stars and Hot Potato points, unlock gemstone slots,
recombobulate its rarity, push enchantments past their normal ceiling, and
reforge it. Upgrade state lives in the item's persistent data container, so
it survives drops, chests, trades, and other plugins rewriting item lore.
Hex stat bonuses are applied as IncogEcon-owned attribute modifiers, and an
item's built-in attributes are preserved so an upgrade never strips a
weapon's base damage.

Essence is earned from a configurable per-mob drop table or bought with
coins, is stored in hex-essence.yml, and is covered by autosave, saveAllData
and /marketadmin reload.

Compatibility with other gear plugins is handled by an optional hook layer
under hex/integration. There are no new build dependencies: every hook is
pure reflection, probes for the other plugin's own API, and stays inactive
when that plugin is missing or its API is not recognised.

- EcoArmor: reads set, tier and advancement state, and adds Hex-paid tier
  and advancement upgrades applied through EcoArmor's own API, with an
  automatic refund when EcoArmor refuses the change.
- Reforges (Auxilor): when installed it provides the reforge list and
  applies reforges; IncogEcon's native reforge table is the fallback.
- MMOItems, EcoItems, ItemsAdder, Oraxen and Nexo items are recognised, and
  protect-unknown-custom-items keeps the Hex off items it cannot upgrade
  safely.

/hex compat and a startup log line report which hooks are active.

Menus are rebuilt on a shared GuiTheme: consistent titles, borders, button
call-to-actions, stat lines, progress bars and navigation items, with
unavailable controls greyed out and explained instead of hidden. Slot
positions, click behaviour and gui-layout.yml are unchanged, and the Hex
follows the existing cross-platform rules of single left clicks and chat
input only.

Version bumped to 1.9.0 with docs, config and changelog updated.

